mover
# The paper schedule's switch (ADR 0050). The first line is the value; the rest is this note.
#   off    a scheduled firing skips by name and places nothing
#   mover  a scheduled firing runs only with --mover among its arguments, and is refused by name without
# `mise run paper:session` reads it at every scheduled firing, from the main that firing cloned, before it
# takes a lock; a run by hand does not read it. `scripts/automation status` shows each firing's outcome.
# The first line is the value and nothing else: any other first line, or no file, fails every scheduled
# firing by name. `mover` needs a plist that carries --mover; scripts/test-lanes checks that the one
# scripts/automation writes does.
